      "math_academy_id": "e-8217",
      "problem": "What is the trace in the $xz$-plane of the elliptic cone $3x^2 +  4y ^2=12(z+3)^2\\: ?$",
      "worked_solution": "To find the trace in the $xz$-plane, we substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}+4\\cdot {0}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ 3{x}^{2} & =12(z+3)^{2} \\\\ {x}^{2} & =4(z+3)^{2} \\\\ \\pm x & =2(z+3) \\\\ \\pm \\frac{x}{2} & =z+3 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\frac{x}{2}-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two lines in the $xz$-plane with equations $z = \\pm\\dfrac{x}{2}-3.$",
